Usage example:

```tsx
<CheckoutScreen
  items={cartItems}
  deliveryFee={5}
  currency="USD"
  onBack={() => navigate("/cart")}
  onPay={({ address, total }) => {
    // call your backend / Telegram payment flow here
  }}
/>
```

A few integration notes:
- CSS variables like `--tg-theme-bg-color` come from Telegram's `WebApp.themeParams`; you'd set them as CSS custom properties on `document.documentElement` on app init (e.g. `document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--tg-theme-bg-color', theme.bg_color)`).
- Validation runs on blur and on submit; the Pay button is disabled when the cart is empty or `isSubmitting` is true.
- `onPay` hands back the validated address and computed total, so you can plug in `Telegram.WebApp.openInvoice` or your own payment API in the caller.
